    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010288</IRI>
        <Literal>C0014472</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010289</IRI>
        <Literal>D020546</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010289</IRI>
        <Literal>Fourth_Ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010289</IRI>
        <Literal>An irregularly shaped cavity in the RHOMBENCEPHALON, located between the MEDULLA OBLONGATA; the PONS; and the isthmus in front, and the CEREBELLUM behind. It is continuous with the central canal of the cord below and with the CEREBRAL AQUEDUCT above, and through its lateral and median apertures it communicates with the SUBARACHNOID SPACE.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010289</IRI>
        <Literal>Fourth Ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010289</IRI>
        <Literal>C0149556</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010290</IRI>
        <Literal>D020547</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010290</IRI>
        <Literal>Lateral_Ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010290</IRI>
        <Literal>Cavity in each of the CEREBRAL HEMISPHERES derived from the cavity of the embryonic NEURAL TUBE. They are separated from each other by the SEPTUM PELLUCIDUM, and each communicates with the THIRD VENTRICLE by the foramen of Monro, through which also the choroid plexuses (CHOROID PLEXUS) of the lateral ventricles become continuous with that of the third ventricle.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010290</IRI>
        <Literal>Lateral ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010290</IRI>
        <Literal>C0152279</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010291</IRI>
        <Literal>D020542</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010291</IRI>
        <Literal>Third_Ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010291</IRI>
        <Literal>A narrow cleft inferior to the CORPUS CALLOSUM, within the DIENCEPHALON, between the paired thalami. Its floor is formed by the HYPOTHALAMUS, its anterior wall by the lamina terminalis, and its roof by EPENDYMA. It communicates with the FOURTH VENTRICLE by the CEREBRAL AQUEDUCT, and with the LATERAL VENTRICLES by the interventricular foramina.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010291</IRI>
        <Literal>Third Ventricle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010291</IRI>
        <Literal>C0149555</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010293</IRI>
        <Literal>D000077502</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010293</IRI>
        <Literal>Glymphatic_System</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010293</IRI>
        <Literal>A vascular waste clearance system in the brain analogous to the lymphatic system that facilitates transporting of solutes and waste products from CEREBROSPINAL FLUID (CSF) and brain INTERSTITIAL FLUID (ISF). CSF from the SUBARACHNOID SPACE enters the brain periarterial spaces, into the interstitium via channels (e.g., AQUAPORIN 4 PROTEIN) on astrocytic endfeet and exchanges with brain ISF before perivenous drainage of solutes and waste.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010293</IRI>
        <Literal>Glymphatic System</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010293</IRI>
        <Literal>C4704774</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010294</IRI>
        <Literal>D008032</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010294</IRI>
        <Literal>Limbic_System</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010294</IRI>
        <Literal>A set of forebrain structures common to all mammals that is defined functionally and anatomically. It is implicated in the higher integration of visceral, olfactory, and somatic information as well as homeostatic responses including fundamental survival behaviors (feeding, mating, emotion). For most authors, it includes the AMYGDALA; EPITHALAMUS; GYRUS CINGULI; hippocampal formation (see HIPPOCAMPUS); HYPOTHALAMUS; PARAHIPPOCAMPAL GYRUS; SEPTAL NUCLEI; anterior nuclear group of thalamus, and portions of the basal ganglia. (Parent, Carpenter&apos;s Human Neuroanatomy, 9th ed, p744; NeuroNames, http://rprcsgi.rprc.washington.edu/neuronames/index.html (September 2, 1998)).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010294</IRI>
        <Literal>Limbic System</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010294</IRI>
        <Literal>C0023715</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010295</IRI>
        <Literal>D009833</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010295</IRI>
        <Literal>Olfactory_Pathway</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010295</IRI>
        <Literal>Set of nerve fibers conducting impulses from olfactory receptors to the cerebral cortex. It includes the OLFACTORY NERVE; OLFACTORY BULB; OLFACTORY TRACT; OLFACTORY TUBERCLE; ANTERIOR PERFORATED SUBSTANCE; and OLFACTORY CORTEX.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010299</IRI>
        <Literal>D019580</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010299</IRI>
        <Literal>Perforant_Pathway</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010299</IRI>
        <Literal>A pathway of fibers that originates in the lateral part of the ENTORHINAL CORTEX, perforates the SUBICULUM of the HIPPOCAMPUS, and runs into the stratum moleculare of the hippocampus, where these fibers synapse with others that go to the DENTATE GYRUS where the pathway terminates. It is also known as the perforating fasciculus.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010299</IRI>
        <Literal>Perforant Pathway</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010299</IRI>
        <Literal>C0524810</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010356</IRI>
        <Literal>D016548</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010356</IRI>
        <Literal>Prosencephalon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010356</IRI>
        <Literal>The anterior of the three primitive cerebral vesicles of the embryonic brain arising from the NEURAL TUBE. It subdivides to form DIENCEPHALON and TELENCEPHALON. (Stedmans Medical Dictionary, 27th ed)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010356</IRI>
        <Literal>Prosencephalon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010356</IRI>
        <Literal>C0085140</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010357</IRI>
        <Literal>D004027</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010357</IRI>
        <Literal>Diencephalon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010357</IRI>
        <Literal>The paired caudal parts of the PROSENCEPHALON from which the THALAMUS; HYPOTHALAMUS; EPITHALAMUS; and SUBTHALAMUS are derived.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010357</IRI>
        <Literal>Diencephalon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010357</IRI>
        <Literal>C0012144</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010358</IRI>
        <Literal>D019261</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010358</IRI>
        <Literal>Epithalamus</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010358</IRI>
        <Literal>The dorsal posterior subdivision of the diencephalon. The epithalamus is generally considered to include the habenular nuclei (HABENULA) and associated fiber bundles, the PINEAL BODY, and the epithelial roof of the third ventricle. The anterior and posterior paraventricular nuclei of the thalamus are included with the THALAMIC NUCLEI although they develop from the same pronuclear mass as the epithalamic nuclei and are sometimes considered part of the epithalamus.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010358</IRI>
        <Literal>epithalamus</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010358</IRI>
        <Literal>C0152361</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010359</IRI>
        <Literal>D019262</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010359</IRI>
        <Literal>Habenula</Literal>
