        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010502</IRI>
        <Literal>Uncrossed tracts of motor nerves from the brain to the anterior horns of the spinal cord, involved in reflexes, locomotion, complex movements, and postural control.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010502</IRI>
        <Literal>extrapyramidal tract</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010502</IRI>
        <Literal>C0015372</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010503</IRI>
        <Literal>D011712</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010503</IRI>
        <Literal>Pyramidal_Tract</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010503</IRI>
        <Literal>Fibers that arise from cells within the cerebral cortex, pass through the medullary pyramid, and descend in the spinal cord. Many authorities say the pyramidal tracts include both the corticospinal and corticobulbar tracts.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010503</IRI>
        <Literal>Pyramidal tract</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010503</IRI>
        <Literal>C0034229</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010504</IRI>
        <Literal>D066148</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010504</IRI>
        <Literal>Spinal_Cord_Dorsal_Horn</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010504</IRI>
        <Literal>One of three central columns of the spinal cord. It is composed of GRAY MATTER spinal laminae I-VI.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010504</IRI>
        <Literal>Spinal Cord Dorsal Horn</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010504</IRI>
        <Literal>C0228575</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010505</IRI>
        <Literal>D020671</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010505</IRI>
        <Literal>Posterior_Horn_Cell</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010505</IRI>
        <Literal>Neurons in the SPINAL CORD DORSAL HORN whose cell bodies and processes are confined entirely to the CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM. They receive collateral or direct terminations of dorsal root fibers. They send their axons either directly to ANTERIOR HORN CELLS or to the WHITE MATTER ascending and descending longitudinal fibers.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010505</IRI>
        <Literal>Posterior Horn Cell</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010505</IRI>
        <Literal>C0752062</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="unti:MeSH_Unique_ID"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010506</IRI>
        <Literal>D013376</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010506</IRI>
        <Literal>Substantia_Gelatinosa</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#04010506</IRI>
        <Literal>Gelatinous-appearing material in the dorsal horn of the spinal cord, consisting chiefly of Golgi type II neurons and some larger nerve cells.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
