        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>http://www.semanticweb.org/fangli/ontologies/2019/2/untitled-ontology-107#11040000</IRI>
        <Literal>Non-specific white matter changes in the BRAIN, often seen after age 65. Changes include loss of AXONS; MYELIN pallor, GLIOSIS, loss of ependymal cells, and enlarged perivascular spaces. Leukoaraiosis is a risk factor for DEMENTIA and CEREBROVASCULAR DISORDERS.

From MSH</Literal>
