        <Literal>Social_Conflict</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#07020983</IRI>
        <Literal>Social_Disorder</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#07020984</IRI>
        <Literal>Social_Integration</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <Annotation>
            <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="x_1.1:source"/>
            <Literal>UMLS</Literal>
        </Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:definition"/>
        <IRI>#07020984</IRI>
        <Literal>A dynamic and principled process where all members participate in dialogue to achieve and maintain peaceful social relations. It does not include coerced assimilation or forced integration. (from https://www.un.org/esa/socdev/sib/peacedialogue/soc_integration.htm) (MSH)
 Process of uniting diverse groups (e.g., racial, ethnic, religious, or disabled) of a society or organization. (PSY)
 Incorporation as equals into society or an organization of individuals of different groups. (CSP)
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0597478</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="core:exactMatch"/>
        <IRI>#07020984</IRI>
        <Literal>Social Integration</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#UMLS_CUI"/>
        <IRI>#07020984</IRI>
